WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.500
When working with documents, there may be
some information that you wish to display

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.330
consistently throughout the documents.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:10.470
So if you had 20 pages, you may want
to have the date and the company logo

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.380
on every page and also page numbers.

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:17.940
To do that, you would use the headers
and footers section of the document.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:21.810
Now the headers and footers
aren't displayed by default.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.900
You have to actually access
them to enter the information.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.740
So to do that, as you can see,
I have a blank document on the

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:32.810
screen, and there are two ways of
accessing the headers and footers.

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:39.269
You can go to the insert tab which
brings up the insert tool bar and

00:00:39.269 --> 00:00:41.550
then select header and footer.

00:00:43.215 --> 00:00:46.065
And alternatively, you can
just click in the document.

00:00:46.065 --> 00:00:48.975
And if I just double click at
the very, very top, it will

00:00:48.975 --> 00:00:50.325
automatically open the header.

00:00:50.894 --> 00:00:53.925
And then I can decide what I
wish to put in to the header.

00:00:54.405 --> 00:00:57.605
And for an example, I'm going
to insert the date and time.

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:03.015
So if I select the date and time
icon, I'm going to select which

00:01:03.015 --> 00:01:07.095
format that I want it to display in
and I'll select the second one down.

00:01:07.725 --> 00:01:09.675
So I select that one there.

00:01:10.515 --> 00:01:13.905
And that will give me
the date in the header.

00:01:16.335 --> 00:01:19.965
The beauty of using the headers and
footers is that when you make changes or

00:01:19.965 --> 00:01:24.825
you move further down the page and the
document size increases, so if I scroll

00:01:24.825 --> 00:01:28.185
down and just move on to another page.

00:01:28.905 --> 00:01:32.505
As you can see, it's automatically
entered the date onto that page.

00:01:33.405 --> 00:01:37.965
Similarly, if I wish to add page
numbers, I would just scroll

00:01:37.965 --> 00:01:39.315
to the bottom of the document.

00:01:39.315 --> 00:01:45.165
And again, I can go to the insert tab or
I can just double click right at the very

00:01:45.165 --> 00:01:50.325
bottom of the document, which will open
the footer and then I can add page number.

00:01:50.505 --> 00:01:56.065
So I select page number and then I would
obviously select the alignments, so do I

00:01:56.085 --> 00:01:59.865
want align to the right, center or left?

00:01:59.895 --> 00:02:01.695
And I want to go for the center.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:04.260
Select OK.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:07.530
And that will insert a page
number into the footer.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:11.189
And as you can see, that is
carried through on every page.

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:18.370
You can access the headers and footers
at any time so I can click away from that

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:23.070
and then work on my document, perhaps
I wanted to make a change to the date

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:27.870
format so I could just double click back
into that, highlight the date format and

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.065
select a different way of displaying it.

00:02:30.065 --> 00:02:30.335
Select OK.

00:02:30.335 --> 00:02:33.328
And that will change that.

00:02:33.748 --> 00:02:37.258
And again, if I wanted to change
how the footer or the page number

00:02:37.258 --> 00:02:41.613
in the footer is displayed, l could
double-click in the footer, highlight

00:02:42.118 --> 00:02:49.998
the number and select page number it
may be that I want to right align that.

00:02:50.773 --> 00:02:53.623
Select OK and that will
automatically right align it.

00:02:54.253 --> 00:02:59.613
You can also insert images and other
information into the header as required.

